% the_burn - blast them dead on ground that burns
%
% The need is a dead enemy. This way of meeting it: find ground whose
% feature reacts lethally with some element (the oil the level laid down is
% the primer), bring the enemy there, make sure it is exposed, bring
% whoever else can be brought, and have someone put the element down. One
% match, one fire. The reaction consumes the feature - after the burn there
% is nothing left to freeze or to burn again. Who brings them in is decided
% by who holds a pull, a push or a dash; who lights it by who holds fire.

theBurn(?e) :-
    if(role(?e, enemy), not(status(?e, dead)),
       regionHas(?r, ?feat), blast(?el, ?feat, dead), reacts(?el, ?feat, ?new),
       not(immune(?e, ?el))),
    do(bringTo(?e, ?r), expose(?e), try(gatherOthers(?e, ?r)), castElement(?el, ?r)).

% Every other living enemy that can be brought in and exposed, is.
gatherOthers(?e, ?r) :-
    allOf, if(role(?o, enemy), \==(?o, ?e), not(status(?o, dead)), not(at(?o, ?r))),
    do(bringTo(?o, ?r), expose(?o)).
